
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html




Step 1: Generate a ROOT_CA Certificate

    1. Generate a private key for the CA:
    openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out ca.key

    2. Create a self-signed CA certificate:
    openssl req -new -x509 -days 3650 -key ca.key -out ca.crt
    // set CN of root_ca to localhost

Step 2: Generate a Server Certificate for Mosquitto

    1. Create a private key for the Mosquitto broker:
    openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out server.key

    2. Generate a Certificate Signing Request (CSR):
    openssl req -new -key server.key -out server.csr
    // set the CN of server certificate to the IP address of the broker

    3. Sign the server certificate with the CA:
    openssl x509 -req -in server.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial \
  -out server.crt -days 3650
